From: ericek111 <erik.brocko@letemsvetemapplem.eu>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:22:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/47] VM display arms itself: no sysctls, no WindowServer
 restart

WindowServer starts before the Auxiliary KC loads and waits for a quiet registry before it looks for displays; once
quiet it opens the framebuffer itself, on its own thread. Arming follows that:

- NMXVGAFB holds the registry busy from start() until the accelerator has armed the head (cap 20 s), and no longer
  sleeps 10 s in start() waiting for an IONDRVFramebuffer that cannot attach (this driver holds the category).
- NMXAccel phase 1 (thread call when the VM display publishes): scan-out and aperture gates, display-pipe
  transactions, MetalPluginName/IOGLBundleName, debug.nvaccelfb reads 1 (the plugin admits WindowServer), the AGDC
  object (NMXAGDC, K5 answers on); then it releases the hold through nmxDisplayReady.
- Phase 2 (NMXVGAFB::open, synchronously, on WindowServer's thread): found_framebuffer, mode change and
  framebuffer_did_power_on, so the head has its display pipe when WindowServer's open returns. Registering before
  open() faulted in IOFramebuffer::getAttributeExt.
- The plugin-name withhold in start() takes the registration lock and skips itself once phase 1 armed.
- NMXAGDC (gen.py): the loader publishes itself and answers nmxAgdcUp.

Measured: WindowServer released 0.2 s after the kexts load; open -> phase 2 -> pipe active; transactions flow from
the boot-time WindowServer with no restart. Without NMXGPU the hold runs out at 20 s and WindowServer goes on.

